00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Ok, let's start from the beginning, so when the ACUs were wired to all the sensors and

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
actuators and motors in the vehicle in order to provide functions.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Each sensor and actuator were connected and wired to an ACU will have more weight and

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000
costs for the vehicle, so there was the necessity to wire together also the ACUs to minimize

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
the number of wires needed in a vehicle.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,000
So, the ACUs started to send and receive data via network.

7
00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000
The need for a robust and stable communication protocol raises because in modern vehicles

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,000
there is the need to connect a large number of ACUs to each other and there is the necessity

9
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,000
to connect also ACUs that are safety relevant for the driver.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:19,000
So, no information loss should happen during this communication.

11
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:28,000
For example, the braking ACUs could not detect wheels that are spinning, that are slipping

12
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:35,000
and signal it to the ACUs that can, to the engine control units that can temporarily reduce

13
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,000
the torque output.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:43,000
This is relevant information for the safety of the drivers, so we must be sure that this

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
information shared via network is not corrupted in any way.

16
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:56,000
