So, we are recording.

22
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Okay.

23
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:19,000
So, networks and network protocols allow the ECU to share information quickly with the reduced

24
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
risk of undetected errors.

25
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Of course, this communication network must be robust in terms also of EMC immunity, electromagnetic

26
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
disturbed immunity.

27
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:43,000
For example, the ignition system used for the combustion engines can create a lot of interference,

28
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:54,000
and so we need to design special vehicle technologies, and the use of a digital communication bus means

29
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:01,000
that this interference can be detected and corrected automatically.

30
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:12,000
The network used between ECU and the vehicle EE systems are based on serial digital communication.

31
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:21,000
So, to meet all those needs, CAN network was developed, and it is the most used one in the automotive field.

32
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:34,000
We will also see that the LIM network, the second type of network we will face today, is, let me say, a more economic alternative to the CAN.

33
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Okay.

34
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Let's go deep into the CAN network.

35
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:48,000
CAN, C-A-N, is an autonomous, used for controller area network, also known as CAN bus.

36
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:53,000
It is a serial standard bus, mainly used in the automotive field.

37
00:03:53,000 --> 00:04:07,000
The CAN communication protocol is a multicast type, used to connect different electronic ECU, electronic control unit, that from now we will call ACU, in the vehicle.

38
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:20,000
The CAN has been especially designed to operate without any problems, even in an electromagnetically disturbed environment, as the vehicle can be used to the interconnection of a lot of ACU sensors,

39
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
actuators, antennas, because it uses a balanced differential potential line.

40
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:36,000
So, uh, and EMC noise immunity can be also, um, increased by using a twisted layer of cables.

41
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
I don't think so.

